<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Nagpur Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1739 CE – 1853 CE (approx.) · capital Nagpur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Maratha kingdom of the Bhonsles of Nagpur, which raided Bengal, ruled Orissa and was annexed by the British under the doctrine of lapse.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raghuji-i-bhonsle">Raghuji Bhonsle</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> general, was sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berar">Berar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gondwana-india">Gondwana</a> and around 1739 established himself at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a>, absorbing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gond-people">Gond</a> kingdom of Deogarh. His armies invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> repeatedly in the 1740s, and in 1751 Nawab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alivardi-khan">Alivardi Khan</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> to him.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhonsles">Bhonsles</a> were among the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> houses, often rivals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a>, and ruled a large but thinly populated realm of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raghuji-ii-bhonsle">Raghuji II</a> was defeated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scindias">Scindia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-assaye">Assaye</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-argaon">Argaon</a> in 1803 and lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berar">Berar</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-deogaon">Treaty of Deogaon</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudhoji-ii-bhonsle">Appa Sahib's</a> attack on the British at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sitabuldi">Sitabuldi</a> in 1817 led to the loss of more land and close British control.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raghuji-iii-bhonsle">Raghuji III</a> died without a son in 1853, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-dalhousie">Lord Dalhousie</a> annexed the kingdom under the doctrine of lapse. Its lands formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur-province">Nagpur Province</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nagpur-kingdom.jpg" alt="Nagpur Kingdom" width="320" height="373"><figcaption>Image: Joseph E. Schwartzberg · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhonsle_kingdom_of_Nagpur.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1739 CE – 1853 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nagpur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Raghuji Bhonsle, Raghuji II, Raghuji III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bhonsles of Nagpur, Kingdom of Nagpur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1796&amp;focus=nagpur-kingdom" aria-label="Nagpur Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6806 1396 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nagpur Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7126 1652L7226 2184M7126 1652L7079 1531M7126 1652L7370 1589M7126 1652L6991 1757M7126 1652L7364 1601M7126 1652L7219 1727M7126 1652L7196 1683"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7226 2184h0M7079 1531h0M7370 1589h0M6991 1757h0M7364 1601h0M7219 1727h0M7196 1683h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7126 1652h0"/><path class="map-dot-me